I would be interested to know what languages do without comparatives -- I
had assumed they were, loosely speaking, semantic universals. The closest
thing I know to "no comparatives" is the Kumeyaay languages, which has been
said to be without them. But if you ask a Kumeyaay speaker what he or she
would say to express the concept that Bill is taller than Tom, you will get
the following construction: Bill is tall; Tom is tall; Bill wins.

